LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Public Tour: Nature-inspired Art
DESCRIPTION:The tour visits three floors of the museum\, looking at a var
 iety of nature-inspired artworks from global cultures\, including nature-
 inspired photography in the featured exhibition The Photographic Reflex: 
 The Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection (https://artmuseum.indian
 a.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html).  Thi
 s tour changes each time\, based on what's on view. Additional tour highl
 ights may include:from the forest of Papa New Guinea\, an artwork made fr
 om natural materials\, representing a leaf spirit\, worn for a night danc
 e  a treasured bowl that held kola nuts\, for welcoming guests to an Afri
 can palace  a sacred object from an indigenous culture (Maori)\, made for
  ocean voyages from a single tree that can live to be 1\,000 years old  a
  large guard\, with ancient origins\, finely crafted\, by a Kenyan artist
 \, into an exquisite food storage container and later repaired  Hand-craf
 ted bamboo baskets from Japan  Paintings of larkspurs\, chrysanthemums\, 
 and more    Plus\, look for signs of nature and discuss the influence of 
 garden experiences on I.M. Pei's iconic architecture.  Each tour may vary
  slightly\, depending on the tour guide.Know Before You GoAdmission and t
 ours are free.Check in with Guest Services at least 5 minutes before the 
 tour start time\, to claim your reservation. At 1:25 p.m. any unclaimed s
 paces may be given to guests who are waiting for a space.Read about where
  to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.To sa
 ve time at the lockers\, avoid bringing backpacks or large bags.  When Yo
 u ArriveCheck in with Guest Services staff on the first floor by 1:25 p.m
 .Store any backpacks or large bags. Lockers and coatrack are available.Do
  not touch artwork. Be mindful to keep all body parts – and anything yo
 u're carrying – at least 18" (a half meter) away from artwork.Photograp
 hy is welcome\, without flash or selfie stick.If you parked in the IMU pa
 rking lot\, Guest Services can validate your parking voucher for a discou
 nt.    If this page says registration has closed\, this means the waitlis
 t is full.  To request this tour at another time for a group of 6-24 peop
 le\, contact Laura at ematours@iu.edu (mailto:ematours@iu.edu).
