BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
DTSTART:20260911T200000Z
DTEND:20260911T210000Z
LOCATION:GISB
SUMMARY:CAHI Humanities Hangout with Dr. Richard Gunderman
DESCRIPTION:Are you pre-med\, or interested in going into a medical field
  and also interested in doing a major or minor in the humanities?  If so\
 , please join us for a Humanities Hangout on Friday\, September 11\, at 4
  pm in GISB 1118\, with Dr. Richard B. Gunderman\, MD\, PhD.  Dr. Gunderm
 an is a distinguished professor of Radiology\, Pediatrics\, Philanthropy\
 , Philosophy\, and Medical Humanities at the Indiana University School of
  Medicine.  He will answer questions about how his training in the humani
 ties is an important part of his career now as a physician\, professor\, 
 and author of numerous books.  Dr. Gunderman is a dynamic speaker and acc
 laimed teacher—so much so that he received the Indiana University Schoo
 l of Medicine's inaugural Inspirational Educator Award in 2015.  Come see
  how exploring your interests in the humanities can help make you a bette
 r doctor and medical professional!  Pizza will be served.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Are you pre-
 med\, or interested in going into a medical field and also interested in 
 doing a major or minor in the humanities?</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;
 ">  If so\, please join us for a Humanities Hangout on Friday\, September
  11\, at 4 pm in GISB 1118\, with Dr. Richard B. Gunderman\, MD\, PhD.</p
 ><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Dr. Gunderman is a distinguished profess
 or of Radiology\, Pediatrics\, Philanthropy\, Philosophy\, and Medical Hu
 manities at the Indiana University School of Medicine.</p><p style="font-
 weight: 400\;">  He will answer questions about how his training in the h
 umanities is an important part of his career now as a physician\, profess
 or\, and author of numerous books.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Dr.
  Gunderman is a dynamic speaker and acclaimed teacher—so much so that h
 e received the Indiana University School of Medicine's inaugural Inspirat
 ional Educator Award in 2015.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Come see
  how exploring your interests in the humanities can help make you a bette
 r doctor and medical professional!</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Piz
 za will be served.</p>
