 l of Maxwell Hall if it rains). Join us for the following presentations:J
 onathan Schlesinger (History)\, "We Found Elephants!: Reading Chinese Ivo
 ry Figurines with Others at the Eskenazi Museum"John Romey (Musicology)\,
  "The Haunting of Cardinal Mazarin: Concino Concini and the Construction 
 of Cultural Memory"Bret Rothstein (Art History)\, "Bruegel in Solaris in 
 the Viewer"We gratefully acknowledge the financial support of the College
  of Arts and Sciences\, the History Department\, the Musicology Departmen
 t\, and the Robert E. &amp\; Avis Tarrant Burke Lecture Fund in the Depar
 tment of Art History.
